  "body": "Stacked on #2969. Review the [changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/d3443eddc...issue/2962-agie-straight-cutoff).\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds one straight open cutoff to the native wire EDM job files post. It is ported onto the zero-step setup writer of #2984 and onto the #2955, #2964, #2968 and #2969 ports. The old branch wrote its own SBL through `jescript.rs`. That writer is deleted on main, and this port does not use it.\n\n- **Selection (app).** A Wire Contour with `side: left` or `side: right` takes one selected straight wall edge of the full-height retained prism. The edge must cross between opposite stock faces. The whole model must be on the side away from the kerf, inside the stock. The operation must state `both_pieces_restrained` and `stock_centered_in_xy_travel`, have no `start`, and have a run-out `clearance` of 3.6 mm or less (`crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs`). A closed cycle still needs `capture` and a start hole.\n- **New operation fields.** `both_pieces_restrained` and `stock_centered_in_xy_travel` are on `WireContourOp`, the project file (default false, so old files load unchanged), the Passes page and the MCP field list. Every other constructor, including the sketch-chain die of main, states them as false.\n- The goldens that main already has (CCSEP20, DIE20 and the inspection goldens) do not change. Other goldens are listed in \"Goldens moved\". Existing tests pass unchanged.\n- **Routing and separation (post).** `export_with_review` sends a left or right job to `cutoff::prepare`, which returns the ISO line and the setup. The separation rule is: 0.0 for an open cut, 1.0 for a closed cycle. A closed cycle with 0.0 is still refused.\n- **Geometry (post).** The ISO is the nominal line, extended 4 mm into air at each end. The entry and exit points are 3 mm to the waste side of the tail ends. The post checks the stock corners and the centered 350 × 250 mm travel with the 20 mm rough offset plus the wire radius.\n- **Text.** The refusals, the CPS description, the user guide and the `camcraft-mcp` skill row name the open cutoff, beside the reentrant and die text. The guide uses the 20 mm offset row for a cutoff. No new user-facing text uses the vendor name as a feature or post name (#3537).\n- **Examples.** `examples/agie/cutoff-lower.camscript` (`LOWER20`, left) and `examples/agie/cutoff-upper.camscript` (`UPPER20`, right) on original 80 × 60 × 20 mm stock.\n\n## Readings\n\nOffline control import on 2026-11-24 (throwaway clone of `practice-color-ready`; the base image SHA-256 did not change). Evidence (screenshots, J00 plots and the imported CamCraft files) is in the maintainer's notes folder `agie-imports-20261123/LOWER20/` and `UPPER20/`. The head of this PR posts the same bytes.\n\n- Import: ISO and SBL bytes on the control match the CamCraft files. The new piece shows `CUT1 - CCB030[0], stp1+stp2`.\n- Work details: \"open contour\", side Links (LOWER20) or Rechts (UPPER20), Afkortsnede 0.0, Uitlooppunt on. Inloop `stp1` and Uitloop `stp2`. `stp1` is at X−44 Y−3 (LOWER20).\n- FORMALCHECK before TECCUT: one error, `Technologie : te definiëren`.\n- TECCUT header: Dia 0.25, H 20, Ra 0.30, Tkm 1.0, Te 1.5. After the assignment: `CCB030[4], stp1+stp2`, offsets 245, 155, 140 and 134 µm.\n- FORMALCHECK after TECCUT: `Controleresultaat: geen fouten`. With warnings: `Uitgekozen opties : 131072` and `Referentiewaarden : te definiëren` only.\n- GRAFICHECK (J00): four passes, each one crossing of the 88 mm line, in alternate directions. LOWER20 at Y −5.755, −5.845, −5.860 and −5.866. UPPER20 at Y 5.755, 5.845, 5.860 and 5.866. Each pass starts and ends at X±44 Y∓3 in air. These are the values of the earlier control run of this PR. The `PKT` marker 3 mm after the entry is the technology change point, as in the accepted DIE20 plot.\n- Note: when the operator opens `stp2` on the Startpunt page and confirms with OK, the control can store `stp2+stp2`. A run that did not open that page kept `stp1+stp2`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` `agie_safe_setup` (module `cutoff`): `cutoff_setup_matches_the_control_checked_zero_step_open_cut` (golden `crates/post/tests/golden/agie-setup/LOWER20.SBL`), `right_is_the_left_setup_with_the_other_side`, `the_open_cut_shares_the_closed_setup_but_for_its_endpoints`, `endpoints_in_stock_on_one_side_or_out_of_travel_write_no_setup`.\n- `camcraft-post` lib `agie::cutoff_tests`: `the_open_cut_includes_air_tails_wire_and_work_origin_in_travel`, `left_and_right_put_the_approach_on_the_waste_side_of_the_directed_line`, `an_open_cut_posts_zero_steps_and_no_separation_and_a_closed_cut_keeps_one_millimetre`.\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native` (`cutoff` module, the ported PR tests): `a_native_cutoff_has_one_nominal_crossing_and_distinct_air_endpoints` (compares the CLI SBL with the `LOWER20.SBL` golden), `unsafe_or_unconfirmed_cutoffs_publish_no_files`.\n- `camcraft-app` lib `wire_edm_dto`: `cutoff_setup_statements_round_trip_and_old_files_have_neither`. `mcp_wire_contour`: `list_operation_types_and_skill_match_wire_contour_dto_and_tool_law`.\n- `camcraft-ui` `wire_page_tests`: `the_open_cutoff_declarations_apply_and_undo_together`.\n- All #2984, #2955, #2964, #2968 and #2969 tests stay green without changes to their assertions.\n\n## Gate (head `c61014a41`)\n\nThe head merges `origin/main` at `aedd9750c`, which has the fix of #3774.\n\n- `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 525 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (58.5 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test agie_safe_setup`: 12 passed.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree HEAD origin/main`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No physical cut was made.\n- Only straight X- or Y-parallel cuts in 20 mm stock are accepted. Other thicknesses, oblique lines, open polygons, a drilled entry and larger clearances are refused. They have no control data.\n- Heavy lanes were not run (P6).\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native wire EDM job files post accepts one straight open cutoff in 20 mm stock. It writes the zero-step setup with the left or right side, separate entry and exit points in air and no separation. It requires confirmation that both pieces stay clamped and that the stock is centered in the XY travel.\n\n## UI screenshots\n\nThis PR contains the two open-cutoff controls of #2972 on the Wire Contour Passes tab. One pair of images covers all five PRs of the stack. The reviewer rendered the images with the crate's egui_kittest harness.\n\nBefore (main):\n\n![Before: Wire Contour Passes tab on main](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr-2972/wire-open-cutoff-before.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter (with the two cutoff controls):\n\n![After: Wire Contour Passes tab with the two cutoff controls](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/pr-screenshots/pr-2972/wire-open-cutoff-after.png?raw=true)\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nThe golden files below are additions relative to main. This PR changes no golden file that main already has. The goldens CCSEP20 and DIE20 of main do not change.\n\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/agie-setup/LOWER20.SBL` (A): pins the open-cutoff (zero-step, one cut) setup SBL. Added by #2972 of the stack.\n\n## Test layout\n\nThis PR adds no new top-level test binary. The new post setup tests are a module of an existing suite. The test count did not change.\n\n- `crates/post/tests/agie_cutoff_setup.rs` moved to `crates/post/tests/agie_safe_setup/cutoff.rs`. It is the module `cutoff` of the existing suite `agie_safe_setup` (4 tests; the suite now has 12 = 8 + 4). The tests are unchanged except for the golden path (`../golden/`).\n- The Gate map of `agie_safe_setup` covers `camcraft_post::agie_setup`, so the quick gate selects the suite for a change in the setup writer.\n- The app tests of this PR were already the module `cutoff` of `agie_native`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #2962\n",
